# patch: 013-unwired-features-2.1.280
# format: CHUNKED, 2.1.280 ONLY
# description: Record, at runtime, which patches are ABSENT from this build.
#
# 🔴 WHY A PATCH EXISTS TO SAY SOMETHING IS MISSING.
#   005, 010 and 012 could not be re-anchored for 2.1.280 (see
#   PORTING-GUIDE.md). The tempting alternative was to ship them re-contexted
#   onto a best-guess anchor so the set stayed at 11/11. That is precisely the
#   failure mode this project keeps hitting: a patch that APPLIES CLEANLY and
#   silently does nothing. 012's own header records a 2.1.260 instance where a
#   context-only anchor emitted a reference to a different live variable and
#   the feature died behind a try/catch, invisibly.
#   So the gap is made explicit instead. The sidecar reads
#   globalThis.__claudiverseUnwired at startup and logs it, so a seat running
#   this binary SAYS what it cannot do rather than appearing whole.
#
# ⚠️ DELETE THIS PATCH once 005/010/012 are properly ported — leaving it in
#   place after they land would report a lie in the other direction.
diff --git a/_custom/SidecarClient.js b/_custom/SidecarClient.js
index 3480a2b..e7a3935 100644
--- a/_custom/SidecarClient.js
+++ b/_custom/SidecarClient.js
@@ -8,12 +8,24 @@
 //   CLAUDIVERSE_TOKEN  — API bearer token (required)
 //   CLAUDIVERSE_URL    — Server base URL (default: http://localhost:4000)
 //   CLAUDIVERSE_TITLE  — Stable session name (e.g. "decomper"); default: timestamp
 //   CLAUDIVERSE_DEBUG  — "1" for debug logging to /tmp/claudiverse.log
 
 var __claudiverse = (function () {
